Pollen Robotics recorded moves, Apache-2.0. The optional moves package
plays motion files from datasets identified by the package pin. The files
are downloaded at a pinned revision with a sha256 checksum and are never
vendored. The move format and community moves tag are Pollen Robotics':
reachy_mini_community_moves.

Chatterbox Turbo, Apache-2.0. The model is not redistributed here; the
voice manifest records its pinned catalog revision and license check.

StackChan firmware base, MIT. The firmware patches in this repository apply to M5Stack's StackChan firmware and the xiaozhi-esp32
project beneath it; their copyright notices and MIT license text stay with those sources. StackChan is M5Stack's robot. This
project is not made, endorsed or sponsored by M5Stack.

Espressif ESP-SR and ESP-IDF. The wake word and command recognizer, the audio front end and the build framework come from
Espressif; the build downloads them under their own licenses (see THIRD-PARTY.md) and this repository holds none of their files.
This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Espressif.

MuJoCo, Apache-2.0. The optional physics mode of the virtual unit loads the engine's WebAssembly build from a pinned public address when a
person turns it on. The engine is not part of this repository, the firmware or the host program.

Product and company names (M5Stack, StackChan, Espressif, and any others named in these files) are used only to say what this
